  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "Rockers bought standard factory-made motorcycles and stripped them down, tuning them up and modifying them to appear like racing bikes. Their bikes were not merely transport, but were used as an object of intimidation and masculinity projecting them uneasily close to death, an element exaggerated by their use of skull and crossbone-type symbolism. First seen in the United States and then England, the rocker fashion style was born out of necessity and practicality."
